  message: "Closed (FIRST BATCH / T0) by G1 bundle merged as dev d007532a38 (PR #808). ini (section/setting), requirements (requirement x3 sites), and properties (property) set stable_id to the non-canonical composite Symbol.id; they now use the shared make_doc_stable_id factory (canonical sha256:<16hex>), node.id unchanged (still the location key). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: the flipped test_stable_ids in test_ini/test_requirements/test_properties assert stable_id.startswith('sha256:') and id != stable_id. Minimal port keeps node.id byte-identical; the span fold also de-collides same-named siblings the line-less composite could collide. CORRECTION to the filed discussion: 11 offending sites, not 7 (bitbake=4, requirements=3). SCOPE SPLIT (T0/T1 per the item's own identity-axis design): the T0 subset above is default-output-NEUTRAL (all noise-kind symbols) -> safe conformance fix, no scheme concern. The T1 remainder (bitbake variable/task/addtask + bibtex entry) is default-output-OBSERVABLE id churn and is DEFERRED pending a coordinated scheme decision -- see the sibling note. Marking WI-banod done for the T0 batch; the T1 residual is tracked in the discussion for a follow-up."  # a1ba
